# NeuroNook

> NeuroNook (App Store: NeuroNook: Mood Journal) is a private, playful wellness journal and daily mood check-in app for iPhone and iPad, created by independent iOS developer Wesley Keetch (weskcode).

## Overview
- **What it is:** A local-first iOS & iPadOS wellness journal built around nine short, construction-themed mini-games covering six wellness areas (sleep, stress, mood, motivation, social connection, and energy) plus optional journal notes.
- **Who it helps:** Designed especially for people who bounce off blank-page journals or rigid habit trackers—including adults with ADHD, autism, executive dysfunction, or days when words do not come easily.
- **How it works:** Completing a daily check-in adds an illustrated house to a seven-day neighborhood street. Earlier days and notes can be revisited anytime in Calendar and Trends, with JSON and PDF export.
- **Privacy:** No account, no ads, no tracking, and no analytics SDKs of its own. Journal entries stay on-device (optional Live Weather uses Apple WeatherKit with rounded location; optional NeuroNook Plus uses StoreKit/RevenueCat).
- **Platforms & Languages:** iPhone and iPad (iOS 26.0 / iPadOS 26.0 or later), localized in English and Spanish, with Reduce Motion support.
- **Disambiguation:** NeuroNook (`https://neuronook.app/`, App Store ID `6745560129`) is Wesley Keetch's private wellness journal app and is unrelated to "Neuro.Nook: Brain Games" by Epic Genius LLC.

